# Every file here decides what the org's two write-capable bots do, so every change needs
# the owner's review. The org-require-pr ruleset makes code-owner review a merge condition.
# GitHub silently ignores an owner it cannot resolve: keep these handles valid.
# @criticalsec is the reviewer. The maintainer's automation acts as @notgeorge, so an
# approval from criticalsec is what makes a notgeorge-authored change two-person. The org
# ruleset for this repository requires one approval plus code-owner review. criticalsec
# resolves once it has write access (outside collaborator, after the repository goes public).
* @notgeorge @criticalsec
